## Files kept on the server

Satellite requires the certificate files at upgrade time, so the role does not
remove them.

- Certificate material: `{{ satellite_cert_rotate_dir if satellite_cert_rotate_component == 'satellite' else satellite_cert_rotate_capsule_tar_dir }}`
- Pre-change archive of `{{ satellite_cert_rotate_backup_paths | join(', ') }}`: `{{ satellite_cert_rotate_backup_dir }}/pki-{{ satellite_cert_rotate_stamp }}.tar.gz`
- Installer log: `{{ satellite_cert_rotate_backup_dir }}/satellite-installer-{{ satellite_cert_rotate_stamp }}.log`

## Rollback

Re-run the role against this host with the previous certificate, key, and CA
bundle. That is another installer run and another service restart; there is no
in-place undo. If the CA changed and hosts were updated to trust it, rolling
back also means reverting the CA on every one of those hosts.

## Follow-up

{% if satellite_cert_rotate_accept_ca_change | bool %}
The CA was allowed to change on this rotation. Every registered host, every
Capsule, and every integration that pins the old CA must be updated, or it
loses its connection to Satellite. See "Refreshing the self-signed CA
certificate on hosts" in the *Managing hosts* guide.
{% else %}
The certificate authority did not change on this rotation, so registered hosts
need no action.
{% endif %}
